                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The concept of indirect control is delightful—this is the kind of game I absolutely love. So, it gets a \"like\" from me, despite all its issues.\nAnd there are... quite a few of them. The biggest one is that the game runs out of steam rather quickly. The tech tree is exhausted, resources are fully tapped, and every word combination has been tried. All that’s left is to watch the chaos of the world you’ve created, but unfortunately, that gets boring, eventually forcing the Creator to abandon their own world.\n\n7 broken telephones out of 10.",
